    "cost_closing_html":  "About \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}} a bowl\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost) for a dish with four different meats in it. Black beans are the cheapest protein in the store and they are what let this pot carry that much pork without wrecking the math.",
    "shop_smart":  [
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eBeans are the point, not the filler.\u003c/strong\u003e Black beans give this dish its body, its color and a good chunk of its protein, and they cost less per serving than almost anything else you can put in a pot.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eBuy the pork shoulder, use the trimmings.\u003c/strong\u003e Feijoada was built on scraps. Every bit of fat and every bone you throw in makes the gravy richer, so buy bone-in when you can.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eBacon and diced ham are seasoning meats.\u003c/strong\u003e Small amounts of each add smoke and salt through the whole pot. This is where a half pound does the job of two.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eSlow cooker on low is the right setting.\u003c/strong\u003e Eight or nine hours is what turns beans into gravy. Rushing it on high gives you beans in broth, which is not the same dish."
                   ],
    "make_it":  [
                    "Weigh your empty mixing pot and write the number down for portioning later.",
                    "Brown the chopped bacon in a skillet, then use that fat to sear the cubed pork shoulder and the cubed beef chuck roast on all sides. Do it in batches so the meat browns instead of steams.",
                    "Cook the diced onion and minced garlic in the same skillet until soft, scraping up everything stuck to the bottom.",
                    "Move the bacon, seared meats, onion and garlic to the slow cooker along with the diced ham, the drained black beans, the chicken broth, the white vinegar, the bay leaves, ground coriander, salt and black pepper.",
                    "Cook on low for 8 to 9 hours, until the pork shreds under a fork and the beans have gone soft enough to thicken the liquid.",
                    "Mash a scoop of the beans against the side of the crock and stir it back in. That is what turns the broth into gravy.",
                    "Pull out the bay leaves, shred the larger pieces of meat, and cook the rice per the package to serve underneath."
                ],
